# Copy to .env.local for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT against the live backend.
#
# Note the flip introduced by the static conversion: this file no longer holds
# "the built-in default". The built-in default is now the EMPTY value, and this
# template holds the development override.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE — where the browser gets its data.
#
#   unset / empty   read the committed static JSON tree at the same origin
#                   (frontend/public/api/**). THIS IS THE DEPLOYED BEHAVIOUR:
#                   Vercel has no .env.local, so production always takes this
#                   branch and no backend process is involved.
#
#   an origin       talk to the live FastAPI app instead, e.g.
#                   http://localhost:8100. Use this while developing — the
#                   backend stays the reference implementation, and working
#                   against it means you need not re-run the pipeline to see a
#                   data change. The bodies are identical either way (both come
#                   from backend/app/payloads.py); only the URL shape differs,
#                   because a static host cannot select a file with `?res=`.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means it is inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime, so
# changing it needs a rebuild. To exercise the deployed behaviour locally,
# build with the variable unset — see docs/DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:8100
